cpu.c: guard x86-only cpuid helpers for non-x86 targets

The __cpuidex and _xgetbv helpers use x86 inline asm constraints
("=a", cpuid, xgetbv) but are only referenced by the x86
pgm_cpuid implementation, which is already guarded by
__i386__/__x86_64__ (with a generic fallback in #else). On RISC-V
the helpers still get compiled and fail with
"invalid output constraint '=a' in asm".

Move the helpers under the same architecture guard.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: linux-sdk-ai-expert <linux-sdk-ai-expert@linux.alibaba>

--- a/cpu.c
+++ b/cpu.c
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@
 //#define CPU_DEBUG
 
 
-#ifndef _MSC_VER
+#if !defined(_MSC_VER) && (defined(__i386__) || defined(__x86_64__))
 static
 void
 __cpuidex (int cpu_info[4], int function_id, int subfunction_id) {
@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@
     "xgetbv" : "=a"(eax), "=d"(edx) : "c"(xcr));
   return (((uint64_t)(edx)) << 32) | eax;
 }
-#endif
+#endif /* !defined(_MSC_VER) && x86 */
 
 
 #if defined(__i386__) || defined(__x86_64__)
